The single-card class provides the shared design, such as:

Background and border
Rounded corners
Shadow
Spacing
Typography
Hover effects

This is your base component.Your card component should reuse these variables instead of defining its own competing colors, fonts, and design values.

This creates three clear layers:

Global design tokens define your site's colors, typography, spacing, and other shared values.
The base component uses those tokens to establish the common card appearance.
Modifier classes adjust the card's layout or presentation for specific purposes.

In short: build the card once, then use classes such as single-card--icon, single-card--image, single-card--text, and single-card--horizontal to adapt it to different situations. This keeps your HTML reusable, your CSS organized, and your website visually consistent.
